            <H3>Introduction</H3>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>Business-critical and/or time-sensitive =

            information must flow between a company, its business =
partners and=20
            its customers in a timely and reliable manner. As the =
business world=20
            continues its technological evolution, the management of =
information=20
            delivery is becoming more and more challenging. InterComms =
is=20
            designed to help companies easily manage business-critical=20
            information. It effectively links manual or =
application-generated=20
            information with the users of the information across the =
enterprise.=20
            Recipients receive the information they need, on time, at =
the=20
            correct location and in the preferred format. </P>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>InterComms is a flexible information =
delivery=20
            solution, designed to reduce costs and ensure reliability in =

            critical business processes. Information flows seamlessly =
between=20
            the producers and consumers of information, thereby reducing =
the=20
            risk of costly information breakdowns. With InterComms, =
desktop=20
            users can employ a single interface to access all=20
            InterComms-controlled output destinations. Not only can end =
users=20
            send documents, spreadsheets and many other forms of output, =
they=20
            can track job progress, control deliveries to multiple =
destinations=20
            and monitor job-related events. InterComms allows users to =
collect,=20
            process, route, store, distribute, control, publish and view =
the=20
            output generated by business applications.</P>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>InterComms is focused on supporting the =

            organization=92s mission critical information systems. As =
such its=20
            main features are flexibility, maximum thru put, and =
reliability.=20
            InterComms simplifies enterprise output management=20
            (application-generated reports, documents, manual or=20
            application-generated messages, signals and triggers, manual =
or=20
            automated file transfer) through easy-to-use applications =
that=20
            provide centralized control of the enterprise, reducing the=20
            administrative learning curve and the risk of interrupted=20
            operations. By unifying administration, operation and =
support of the=20
            information delivery environment, InterComms allows =
companies to=20
            manage and track output job deliveries and output resources =
more=20
            easily =96 without installing a different product for every =
output=20
            function. You can now incorporate output management as a =
component=20
            of your systems management strategy.</P>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>Using InterComms in conjunction with =
<SPAN=20
            class=3Dvertebraefont>Vertebrae</SPAN>=92s Data Exchange =
Manager, an=20
            application may access and update data stored in remote =
legacy or=20
            relational databases.</P>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>InterComms adds value in terms of =
business=20
            benefits, measurable cost reductions, and offers a =
competitive=20
            advantage:</P>
            <H4><A name=3DBusinessBenefits></A><IMG height=3D24=20
            =
src=3D"file:///D:/InternetDev/Vertebrae/Images/BoneBullet.gif"=20
            width=3D35 align=3DabsBottom> Business Benefits</H4>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>More timely distribution of and faster =
access to=20
            information, customizing of information to individual needs, =
better=20
            customer service, improved internal service levels, and =
assured=20
            delivery of business-critical information; </P>
            <H4><A name=3DCostReductions></A><IMG height=3D24=20
            =
src=3D"file:///D:/InternetDev/Vertebrae/Images/BoneBullet.gif"=20
            width=3D35 align=3DabsBottom> Cost Reductions</H4>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>Device sharing, reduced paper and forms =
costs,=20
            reduced cost of maintenance, reduced shipping costs, reduced =

            telephone and mailing costs, reduced training costs, reduced =
help=20
            desk cost, reduced cost of making changes to output =
requirements;=20
            </P>
            <H4><A name=3DCompetitiveAdvantages></A><IMG height=3D24=20
            =
src=3D"file:///D:/InternetDev/Vertebrae/Images/BoneBullet.gif"=20
            width=3D35 align=3DabsBottom> Competitive Advantages</H4>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>All the benefits listed above plus =
IT/IS=20
            operational excellence, consistency of application of =
policies, less=20
            repetition of work, automation of otherwise manual =
processes,=20
            improved reliability of business-critical information =
delivery=20
            processes, lower error rates, non-disruptive business supply =

            chain.</P>
            <H3><A name=3DHighlights></A>Highlights</H3>
            <H4><A name=3DSendAndForgetMessages></A><IMG height=3D24=20
            =
src=3D"file:///D:/InternetDev/Vertebrae/Images/BoneBullet.gif"=20
            width=3D35 align=3DabsBottom> Send-and-Forget Messages</H4>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>Distributing automated mail-shots, =
staff notices,=20
            client messages and promotions is a breeze using Send and =
Forget=20
            Messages (SFMs). It is the preferred method of sending =
messages when=20
            no response is required. SFMs can be sent to any number of=20
            recipients via email or SMS. You can even use it to =
implement an=20
            alarms system by having your system send you an SFM via SMS =
when=20
            things go wrong.</P>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>InterComms even allows you to take =
action by=20
            issuing commands back to your system by sending SMS messages =
from=20
            your cellular phone. SFMs are ideal for integration into =
your=20
            existing system. Distribute end-of-day results or sales =
figures=20
            generated by your system automatically as soon as they are=20
            generated. </P>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>No more excuses for delays in getting =
the=20
            management information you need when you need it!</P>
            <H4><A name=3DDataTransferWithADifference></A><IMG =
height=3D24=20
            =
src=3D"file:///D:/InternetDev/Vertebrae/Images/BoneBullet.gif"=20
            width=3D35 align=3DabsBottom> Data Transfer with a =
Difference</H4>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>InterComms takes care of all your =
controlled data=20
            and file transfer requirements. It introduces a new level of =

            flexibility in data distribution management by providing a=20
            comprehensive set of tools allowing you to integrate =
InterComms with=20
            your existing systems and infrastructure.</P>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>Let InterComms solve the management =
headaches=20
            associated with time critical transfer tasks, such as =
software or=20
            stock price updates.</P>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>Transfers can be scheduled to make =
optimum use of=20
            bandwidth to alleviate carrier congestion or to make use of =
off peak=20
            communication rates. InterComms ensures total control over =
your data=20
            from point of origin to point of application with delivery =
and=20
            application status reports and complete audit trails. =
Transferred=20
            data can be scheduled to be applied at a future date, with a =

            confirmation message sent to the originator after every step =
in the=20
            transfer and application process.</P>
            <P>In a nutshell:</P>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>InterComms provides convenient data =
transfer=20
            scheduling with just-in-time application capabilities.</P>
            <H4><A name=3DIntegrationAndDestination></A><IMG height=3D24 =

            =
src=3D"file:///D:/InternetDev/Vertebrae/Images/BoneBullet.gif"=20
            width=3D35 align=3DabsBottom> Integration and Destination =
Control Made=20
            Easy!</H4>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>Define any folder on your local machine =
as a=20
            Monitored Folder, set up recipients and destination folders =
and=20
            you=92re ready to go. Any file dropped in a Monitored Folder =
is now=20
            automatically distributed by InterComms and processed by the =

            recipient. Each recipient can receive the files in a =
different=20
            destination folder and use a different transfer =
protocol.</P>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>Folder Monitors provide a simple =
solution to your=20
            complex enterprise wide data distribution requirements =
without the=20
            need to modify your existing systems. </P>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>In fact, it is so simple and efficient =
to use,=20
            you=92ll wonder why you ever considered alternative data =
distribution=20
            methods. </P>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>Using folder monitors you can configure =
unlimited=20
            hopping between your various machines, using different =
protocols for=20
            each hop. </P>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>When used in conjunction with the <SPAN =

            class=3Dvertebraefont>Vertebrae</SPAN> Data Exchange =
Manager,=20
            integration into your existing application is =
straightforward and=20
            easy!</P>
            <H4><A name=3DHaveYourProtocol></A><IMG height=3D24=20
            =
src=3D"file:///D:/InternetDev/Vertebrae/Images/BoneBullet.gif"=20
            width=3D35 align=3DabsBottom> Have Your Protocol and Eat it =
Too!</H4>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>Choose between direct transfer or =
scheduled=20
            transfer, or a combination of these. </P>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>Direct transfers cater for environments =
where a=20
            permanent TCP/IP connection exists between sender and =
recipient.=20
            Timed transfers can, in addition to permanent connections, =
use=20
            Internet dial-up connections to any existing ISP for =
transfers. </P>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>The SMTP and POP3 protocols are used to =
send data=20
            as packaged messages using your existing email =
infrastructure. This=20
            transfer method makes full use of the advantages of email=20
            queuing.</P>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>By using your existing email =
infrastructure, your=20
            communications system need not break the bank due to extra =
costs=20
            incurred.</P>
            <H4><A name=3DGrowingWithYourEnterprise></A><IMG height=3D24 =

            =
src=3D"file:///D:/InternetDev/Vertebrae/Images/BoneBullet.gif"=20
            width=3D35 align=3DabsBottom> Growing with your =
Enterprise</H4>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>InterComms is the last electronic =
communication=20
            and distribution system you will ever need. Unlimited =
scalability=20
            means that InterComms can grow with your business. </P>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>Whether you=92re running the next =
Fortune 1000=20
            company (but for =93technical reasons=94 your current IT =
Department=20
            consists of a single machine) or you=92re already =
contemplating your=20
            own country, use InterComms to keep you on top of your =
business=20
            wherever you are. </P>
            <H4><A name=3DSelectYourAudience></A><IMG height=3D24=20
            =
src=3D"file:///D:/InternetDev/Vertebrae/Images/BoneBullet.gif"=20
            width=3D35 align=3DabsBottom> Select your Audience</H4>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>Any message can be sent to recipient =
groups=20
            within groups, within groups, within=85 Create recipient =
group=20
            profiles and send messages to a selected group (with its sub =
groups)=20
            using each group member=92s default profile settings or to a =
specific=20
            recipient in the shared InterComms Address book.</P>
            <H4><A name=3DBigBrotherWatching></A><IMG height=3D24=20
            =
src=3D"file:///D:/InternetDev/Vertebrae/Images/BoneBullet.gif"=20
            width=3D35 align=3DabsBottom> Big Brother Watching</H4>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>InterComms provides a full audit trail =
of all=20
            communication events. It also provides detailed message =
status=20
            information. A manager or supervisor can retrieve this =
information=20
            irrespective of location by issuing remote commands or =
requests.=20
</P>
            <P class=3Dparagraph>Now, if they say they=92ve sent it, =
they better=20
            have=85</P>
            <H3>Application Examples</H3>
            <H4><IMG height=3D24=20
            =
src=3D"file:///D:/InternetDev/Vertebrae/Images/BoneBullet.gif"=20
            width=3D35 align=3DabsBottom> File and Data Transfer</H4>
            <UL>
              <LI>Consolidate branch day-end results to Head Office=20
              <LI>Post Head Office data (Stock &amp; Debtors) to =
Branches=20
              <LI>Inter-Branch Stock Transfers=20
              <LI>Branch Purchase Orders and Requests=20
              <LI>Software Upgrades=20
              <LI>New Pricing Structures (send now, apply later)=20
              <LI>Inter-Company Data Transfer (orders, prospects, etc.)=20
              <LI>Web-Server Database Updates </LI></UL>
            <H4><IMG height=3D24=20
            =
src=3D"file:///D:/InternetDev/Vertebrae/Images/BoneBullet.gif"=20
            width=3D35 align=3DabsBottom> Promotions, Notices &amp; =
Reminders</H4>
            <UL>
              <LI>Automatic birthday wishes to Clients=20
              <LI>Welcome notices (SMS/email)=20
              <LI>Special offers and promotions=20
              <LI>Reminders of payments due, appointments=20
              <LI>Notification of new jobs, deliveries, pickups, etc.=20
              <LI>Automatic notification of failed payments to clients=20
              <LI>Product launch announcements=20
              <LI>Booking confirmations </LI></UL>
            <H4><IMG height=3D24=20
            =
